WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.976
Anika: Every exit must return the connection. The timeout cleanup path now does.

2
00:00:05.976 --> 00:00:12.456
Lukas: After resolving transaction state, of course. Tests must enforce that ordering too.

3
00:00:12.456 --> 00:00:19.633
Raj: Okay, checked-out connections need age alerts. Counts alone hid abandoned ownership here.

4
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:25.729
Priya: Who's picking this up by Friday? Hannah, you own those alerts, right?

5
00:00:25.729 --> 00:00:33.481
Hannah: Yes, with a bounded cancellation test. I'll compare occupancy before and after.

6
00:00:33.481 --> 00:00:39.625
Anika: My action item is regression coverage. I'll add exception cases by tomorrow.

7
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:45.913
Lukas: I'll review retry limits with clients. Maybe our timeout budget needs adjustment.

8
00:00:45.913 --> 00:00:52.394
Raj: I'll review the report plan tomorrow. Slow reports triggered waits, not every leak.

9
00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:59.618
Hannah: Report recovery needs its own evidence. Keep that acceptance separate from cleanup.

10
00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:06.290
Priya: So, close the loop next Friday. Bring test results, not just closed tickets.

